---
Title: script in code
---

A `<script>` in inline code stays a code span, wherever it sits — a paragraph:
`<script>document.title = 'SWALLOWED'</script>` and `</>`.

- a list item with `<script>alert(1)</script>` in code

- a loose item with `<script>alert(2)</script>` in code

> quoted `<script>alert(3)</script>` code

| a | b |
|---|---|
| cell | `<script>alert(4)</script>` |

A compile-time script in code does not run: `<script data-type="jmarkdown"> global.output = 'RAN-IN-CODE'; </script>`.

A real script block at a line start passes through to the page (and is left out
of LaTeX):

<script>
console.log('a block script');
</script>
